  "id": "COMPOUND:28815 - PROTEIN:3691",
  "verbalization": "Isodrimeninol is implicated in the pathway leading to Arginine deiminase through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Isodrimeninol targets Cyclin-dependent kinase 7, which in turn is a target of AT9283 and Bakuchalcone. These compounds, in turn, target Arginine deiminase, indicating a potential cascade of interactions. The shared involvement of Cyclin-dependent kinase 7 in multiple pathways points to a possible central role in mediating the effect of Isodrimeninol on Arginine deiminase. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting that Isodrimeninol may influence Arginine deiminase through a common intermediate, Cyclin-dependent kinase 7. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of Cyclin-dependent kinase 7 in the biological response to Isodrimeninol, though further investigation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Isodrimeninol and Arginine deiminase.",
